# Rust. Images ship dev-lang/rust-bin (2026-10-01, author's decision): the trunk
# needs a Rust to rebuild mesa, git, librsvg and bindgen, and every one of them
# depends on `|| ( rust-bin rust )` for a slot, so the binary satisfies them all
# without compiling the compiler. Only sys-devel/rust-std (crossdev) and the BPF
# tools (dev-util/bpf-linker, net-proxy/mitmproxy-linux) need the source build;
# none is in an image (checked against the pinned trees).
# dev-lang/rust stays in the library as catalog-only: built for the binhost, so
# whoever wants the source compiler installs it as a binary. D23 (2026-09-26)
# had put it in every image; the measured cost then was 5 packages (rust,
# rust-common, lld-22, oniguruma), bootstrapped from rust-bin.
dev-lang/rust-bin
#dev-lang/rust
